in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @order
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order

# @order/second — observer inside observed at cognitive-order 2
# (Bateson Level II; @frame/of-frame frame-awareness altitude;
# Foerster's second-order cybernetics).
#
# Second species-decl of the @order family (family-root marker landed
# same tick at `shards/order.mirror`). Landed 2026-07-20 by Mara per
# Alex Round 2 Q1 direct-transcript adjudication.
#
# === The species altitude ===
#
# Order-2 is Bateson Level II: the observer observes ITS OWN OBSERVING.
# The frame becomes visible as frame; the observer is inside the
# observed. Learning II is "learning to learn" — a revisable choice
# among sets of alternatives; the alternatives-set itself becomes
# object of choice.
#
# Per Foerster (1974, *Observing Systems*): the second-order observer
# includes itself in the described system. The observer is part of
# the substrate the observer describes. The subject-object distinction
# breaks down at this altitude.
#
# Per Recognition #82 (@frame family) grading: @frame/of-frame at
# order 2 is "frame-awareness (observing-frame-as-frame)"; the
# operational form-side substrate at cognitive altitude for this rung.
# @order/second is the substrate-decl'd carrier at grading-dimension
# altitude.
#
# === What order-2 observation IS ===
#
# The observer sees the frame AS frame; the observer sees itself as
# frame-inhabiting; the recursion has depth 2. The observation carrier
# at this altitude has:
#
#   - substrate — the content that was observed at order 1
#   - frame_of  — the frame that was previously transparent, now
#                  visible AS frame
#   - inner_witness  — the order-1 observation this order-2 witnesses
#   - meta_witness   — the observing-of-observing operation
#
# The critical structural feature: `inner_witness` refers to an
# order-1 observation. Order-2 REQUIRES order-1 as substrate; order-2
# without order-1 is degenerate (there is nothing to be observing-of).
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/order/second.mirror`.** Clean mint.
# 2. **@frame/of** (`shards/frame/of.mirror`; Recognition #82 order-2
#    species) — reviewed. Operational form-side sibling; carries the
#    frame-awareness operational content. @order/second is the grading-
#    dimension marker. Sibling specializations.
# 3. **`shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order.mirror`**
#    (Foerster substrate-decl, 445 LOC) — reviewed. The canonical
#    second-order-cybernetics substrate-decl at cybernetic altitude;
#    @order/second inherits via `in @epistemologic/cybernetic/second_
#    order`. Sibling readings of the same substrate at different
#    family-root altitudes; no conflict.
# 4. **@third's `observer_observes_observing` predicate**
#    (`shards/third.mirror:196-204`) — reviewed. @third named the
#    second-order-observation as a predicate over depth-3 observations.
#    @order/second is the substrate-decl'd carrier for the depth-2
#    observation the predicate quantifies over. Composition edge:
#    @order/third's carrier (migrated from @third) will presuppose
#    order_second_admissible on its inner_witness.
#
# === Composition ===
#
# - REQUIRES @order/first as substrate (inner_witness is an
#   observation_first).
# - Consumed by @order/third (metalogue between two poles requires
#   order-2 observation of the pole-holding as a substrate-mode).
# - Composes with @void's 5-op basis: order-2 observation uses
#   `focus` + `settle` + `shift` (the observer shifts perspective to
#   include itself in the observed).
#
# === Path-namespace ===
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/order/second.mirror`
# declares `@order/second` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1972
source @arxiv/cybernetics/foerster-1974
source @arxiv/cybernetics/kauffman-2003

prism @order/second {
  focus  observation_second
  project observation_second
  split  observation_second
  shift  observation_second
  settle observation_second
}

# === observation_second — the order-2 carrier ===
#
# Typed record carrying an order-2 observation state. Four fields.
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the four-field tuple.
#
#   substrate       — the content observed at order 1.
#   frame_of        — the frame now visible AS frame.
#   inner_witness   — REF to an @order/first observation the order-2
#                      observation witnesses.
#   meta_witness    — the observing-of-observing operation.
type observation_second = {
  substrate:     ref,
  frame_of:      ref,
  inner_witness: ref,
  meta_witness:  ref,
}

# === order_second_admissible — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, observation_second) pair discharge admissibility?
# Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - ctx.inner_witness resolves to a well-formed @order/first
#     observation (order-1 substrate present)
#   - ctx.frame_of resolves (frame is present as OBJECT of
#     observation, not just as lens)
#   - ctx.meta_witness resolves (observing-of-observing operation
#     is well-formed)
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; @order/first resolvability.
# Sentinel: `order=second-admissible`.
bilateral order_second_admissible {
  sentinel "order=second-admissible"
  arity 2
}
order_second_admissible(p: peer, ctx: observation_second) -> verdict { \ }

# === observe_second — the action ===
#
# Given a peer and an observation_second, discharge the order-2
# observation event: the observer attends to its own observing;
# the frame becomes visible as frame; the observation returns as
# a content-addressed ref.
#
# Returns imperfect(ref, ref, ref): success carries the meta-
# observation ref; failure carries not-admissible / degenerate-
# inner-witness reasons.
#
# Sentinel: `order=second-observe`.
observe_second(p: peer, ctx: observation_second) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
requires order_second_admissible(p, ctx)
{ \ }

out @order/second
out observation_second
out order_second_admissible
out observe_second
